---
title: API
order: 4
---

The Compeer API allows you to create custom functionality for your agenetic workflow. All endpoints are served under `/api/v1` and return JSON.

## Endpoints

### GET /api/v1/stores

Returns all stores.

Response:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "7b5f23f7-3c7b-4a8d-9c49-6d7ef4f1324d",
    "name": "My Store"
  }
]
```

### GET /api/v1/search

Searches captures with a required query string and optional store filter.

Query parameters:

- `query` (string, required): Search query.
- `storeId` (string, optional): Limit results to a single store.

Response:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "2c3a6c5d-2d4b-4b52-9f2e-4f07c8b9e3e1",
    "type": "text",
    "content": "Launch checklist",
    "storeId": "7b5f23f7-3c7b-4a8d-9c49-6d7ef4f1324d"
  }
]
```

### POST /api/v1/capture

Creates a new capture.

Fields:

- `type` (string, required): One of `text`, `data`, `url`.
- `content` (string, required): Capture content.
- `storeId` (string, required): Store to attach the capture to.


Request body:

```json
{
  "type": "text",
  "content": "My note",
  "storeId": "7b5f23f7-3c7b-4a8d-9c49-6d7ef4f1324d"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true
}
```
